# Allowlist: ignore everything in this Steam-managed tree, then un-ignore
# only this project's own folders. Keeps stock AC apps and the rest of the
# game out of git.
/*
!/.gitignore

!/CLAUDE.md
# CLAUDE.md's two companions: the full build record it was split from, and the
# open question of how the tolerance bands should be calibrated. This is an
# allowlist, so a new top-level file is invisible to git until it is named here.
!/MILESTONE_LOG.md
!/BAND_CALIBRATION_BRIEF.md
# The reply to BAND_CALIBRATION_BRIEF.md's prompt. Tracked because the brief and
# CLAUDE.md now cite it for claims they do not restate in full -- including which
# of its findings were marked unverified, which is the part a viva would ask
# about. (`trace-litreview-v0.3.md` is still untracked; name it here too if it is
# meant to be kept.)
!/TRACE_tolerance-calibration_lit-review_v1.0.md
# The session-budget brief: the 30-minute participant-time constraint, the three
# protocol shapes costed against it, and the decisions taken (Shape B at 15
# laps, the frozen-g1b recalibration, and the two Gate G1 targets restated).
# CLAUDE.md, evaluation_plan_v2.md and G1_REVIEW.md all cite it for reasoning
# they do not restate. It was written on 2026-10-15 and was silently IGNORED by
# this allowlist for the rest of that session -- which is exactly the failure
# mode the comment above warns about, so it is worth saying twice: a new
# top-level file does not exist as far as git is concerned until it is named
# here, and `git status` will not tell you it is missing.
!/SESSION_BUDGET_BRIEF.md
# The CURRENT thesis framing (2026-10-30). v6 was deleted that day; read it with
#   git show 110156e:thesis_framing_v6.md
# and its last uncommitted edits are in novelty_audit/logs/ as a patch.
!/thesis_framing_v9.md
# The v9 novelty audit: its README is the entry point, CLAIMS_SHEET_v9.md is
# what the thesis may claim. papers_txt/ holds extracted full texts of
# copyrighted papers and must NEVER be tracked; neither may /Academic Papers/
# (already excluded by /* above).
!/novelty_audit/
/novelty_audit/papers_txt/
# Project-scoped Claude Code config: settings.json enables the
# academic-research-skills plugin (CC BY-NC 4.0, installed from its marketplace).
# The llm-council skill is NOT tracked: its source repo
# (github.com/aiwithremy/claude-skills-llm-council) carries no licence, so copy
# it into .claude/skills/llm-council/ by hand on a fresh clone.
# settings.local.json is personal and stays out.
!/.claude/
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/skills/
!/implementation_plan_v2.md
!/evaluation_plan_v2.md
!/DATASET_README.md
!/.github/
!/schemas/
!/configs/
# The controller parity corpus: the only state the runtime and the simulator
# share besides controller_config.json (impl plan section 3), and the artefact
# Gate G1 rests on.
!/golden_traces/
!/kit/
!/lua/
/lua/*
!/lua/projspike_lua/
!/lua/trace_rt/
!/python/
/python/*
!/python/GRApp/

# Noise inside tracked folders
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
